 "text": "Hello there, how's life treating you? That's a common challenge. One way to solve it is to draw a simple eye first, then use it as a guide while you fill in the face. Start with rough shapes, then add details. You can use thin lines of pencil or a light pencil over them. Use very few lines, just enough to stop it from getting too big. You can draw it in the center line, or between two eyeballs if you' drawing two people. Enjoy the process. Drawing is lot of little victories, like getting an eye to stop at the right height, or filling in an ear that looks just like your reference.",
